{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>Is there anything to this beyond a nice walk? Actually, yes. In <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-019-44097-3">a study of nearly 20,000 people</a>, spending at least two hours a week in natural settings was associated with noticeably better health and well-being (White et al., 2019, <em>Scientific Reports</em>). And the coast in particular tends to outperform other settings: follow-up research found coastal visits were linked to the biggest boosts in well-being of any natural environment (White et al., 2021).</p>
  <p>None of that is a promise about your particular Tuesday. It just means the shoreline is a well-worn place to do this kind of work, and the map has been walked before.</p>
